course: dictionary
lesson: 13227
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be a thing in one sentence and an action in the next. Garrison is one of them. Its meaning changes with its job, but the idea of guarding stays the same. Look at the words around it to see which job it is doing.
explain: «The garrison guarded the castle gate all night.» Here a garrison is the group of soldiers, because soldiers are the ones who guard. Now read «The garrison was a small stone fort on the hill.» Here garrison means the fort where the soldiers live.
explain: «The king garrisoned the castle with fifty soldiers.» This time garrison is a verb, a doing word. It means to put soldiers in a place to guard it. Ask yourself: is it a thing, or is it something someone does? That question helps you find the job.
fact: A garrison is a group of soldiers who live in a town or fort to guard it.
fact: A garrison can also mean the fort, castle or town where those soldiers live.
fact: As a verb, «garrison» means to put soldiers in a place to guard it.
fact: The forms are: a garrison, garrisons; to garrison, garrisoned, garrisoning.
fact: In history, Roman forts on Hadrian's Wall had garrisons of soldiers to guard them.
exercise: «The garrison guarded the castle gate all night.» What does garrison mean here? | The name of a king | *The soldiers who guard the castle | A long, thin river | A kind of cake
exercise: «The king garrisoned the castle with fifty soldiers.» What kind of word is garrisoned here? | A thing (noun) | A joining word | *A doing word (verb) | A describing word
exercise: «The soldiers marched back to the garrison before dark.» Which word means the place where the soldiers live? | soldiers | *garrison | before | marched
test: «The garrison surrendered after the long siege.» What did the garrison do? | *Gave up to the enemy | Built a new wall | Sang a song for the king | Went home to bed
test: «The general wanted to garrison the old fort before winter.» What does garrison mean here? | To cook a big meal | To paint the walls white | To run away quickly | *To put soldiers in the fort to guard it
exam: «The garrison town was quiet until the enemy arrived.» What is a garrison town? | A town full of farms | A town with the biggest shops | A town by the sea with no roads | *A town where soldiers live to guard it
